course: dictionary
lesson: 184
title: The accent aigu
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Aigu is a French word, not an English one. It means «sharp» or «high». In French, the accent aigu is the little mark that slopes up to the right on the letter é.
explain: The names of French accents describe their shapes: aigu means sharp, grave means low, and circonflexe means bent around. Cédille is said "say-DEE-y" and tréma is said "tray-MA".
explain: The accent aigu changes how the letter e sounds. «Le café» is said "ka-FAY", and «l'école» (school) is said "lay-KOL". Look for the sloping mark on é, and the e will say "ay".
fact: Aigu is a French word that means «sharp» or «high».
fact: The accent aigu (é) is the mark that slopes up to the right.
fact: The accent aigu makes the letter e say "ay", as in «le café».
fact: The other French accents are grave (è), which means low, and circonflexe (ê), which means bent around.
fact: To an English ear, aigu sounds like "ay-GOO", with the French u said with rounded lips.
exercise: In French, aigu means which of these? | Bent around | Low and deep | *Sharp or high | Hidden
exercise: Which accent is on the e in «le café»? | Circonflexe | Cédille | *Aigu | Grave
exercise: In «le café», the accent aigu makes the e say which sound? | Ee, as in "see" | Oo, as in "moon" | It is silent | *Ay, as in "ka-FAY"
test: What does grave mean in the names of French accents? | *Low | Sharp | Heavy | Bent around
test: Is aigu an English word? | *No, it is a French word | Yes, it is a type of bird | Yes, it means round | Yes, it is common in English
exam: In «l'école» (school), which letter has the accent aigu? | ê | è | *é | ç
